\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B3.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mSlow down near the station.\u001b[34G\u001b[22mArrive\u001b[41Gslowly\u001b[48Genough\u001b[55Gto\u001b[58Gstop\u001b[63Gwell\u001b[68Gshort\u001b[74Gof\u001b[77Ganything.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B4\u001b[6G\u001b[1mLapse a pad only when \u001b[29Ghe ship isn't progressing.\u001b[22m Then a\u001b[63Gslow\u001b[68Gbut working arrival\u001b[88Gkeeps\u001b[94Gits\u001b[98Gpad,\u001b[103Gand\u001b[107Ga\u001b[109Gstuck\u001b[115Gone\u001b[119Gis\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gdropped.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWhat I'd do for us:\u001b[23G\u001b[22mthe\u001b[27Gfirst\u001b[33Gtechnique,\u001b[44Gin\u001b[47GJettison's\u001b[58Gdocks.\u001b[65GAdd\u001b[69Gan\u001b[72Gapproach\u001b[81Gpoint\u001b[87Gon\u001b[90Gthe\u001b[94Gpad's\u001b[100Gnormal,\u001b[108Gbeyond\u001b[115Gthe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Babove-pad point by mor\u001b[27Gthan th\u001b[35G sh\u001b[39Gp's braking distance. The\u001b[65Ginbou\u001b[71Gd course goes \u001b[86Ghroug\u001b[92G it, so\u001b[100Gthe last leg is\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bstraight down \u001b[18Ghe normal, \u001b[31Gd the 10 m ma\u001b[45Ggin can \u001b[56Gy as\u001b[61Git is. This\u001b[73Gremov\u001b[79Gs the\u001b[85Gsideways overshoot\u001b[104Gtha\u001b[109Gthe\u001b[113G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bavoidance kept pumping, rather than moving t\u001b[76Gses.\u001b[81GIt i\u001b[86G still a fix inside our own\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.334, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gdon't land in time; that's the same role as \u001b[51Gr res\u001b[57Grvation. A speed limit a\u001b[82Gplies near th\u001b[96G stat\u001b[104G, \u001b[107Gnd the docking\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bc\u001b[7Gmputer fl\u001b[17Ges a fixed approach in through the entrance.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mGeneral autopilot (Space Engineers):\u001b[22m the remote-control autopilot\u001b[71Gis\u001b[74Gknown\u001b[80Gfor\u001b[84Gcircling\u001b[93Gor\u001b[96Govershooting\u001b[109Gits\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gwaypoints. Players work around it with a\u001b[46Gslow precisi\u001b[59Gn\u001b[61Gmode or \u001b[70Gheir own scripts. That\u001b[93Gis\u001b[97Gur failure,\u001b[109Gand\u001b[113Gthe\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Breas\u001b[10Gn \u001b[13Ghe\u001b[16Gothers constr\u001b[30Gin the last leg.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BThese\u001b[9Ggames\u001b[15Gcombine\u001b[23Gfour\u001b[28Gtechniques:\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B1. \u001b[1mMake the final approach one-dimensional.\u001b[47G\u001b[22mBring\u001b[53Gthe\u001b[57Gship\u001b[62Gto\u001b[65Ga\u001b[67Gpoint\u001b[73Gout\u001b[77Galong\u001b[83Gthe\u001b[87Gpad's\u001b[93Gnormal\u001b[100Gand\u001b[104Gcome\u001b[109Gin\u001b[112Gstraight,\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gso any overshoot heads toward or away from the\u001b[53Gstation rather than\u001b[73Gsideways into\u001b[87Gan orbit.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B2.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mDon't treat the destination as an obstacle on the final leg.\u001b[22m We \u001b[71Glrea\u001b[76Gy do this when descending\u001b[102G(\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mbyHull\u001b[39m),\u001b[112Gbut\u001b[116Gnot\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gon the inbound leg.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B3.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mSlow down near the station.\u001b[34G\u001b[22mArrive\u001b[41Gslowly\u001b[48Genough\u001b[55Gto\u001b[58Gstop\u001b[63Gwell\u001b[68Gshort\u001b[74Gof\u001b[77Ganything.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B4\u001b[6G\u001b[1mLaps