[0.071, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[20B\u001b[38;2;225;139;107mSmooshing…\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.079, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 141 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  What other games do, from recollection and not checked against sources: EVE has no approach,        \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 142 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  docking at once within range; Freelancer and many older games fly to a ring or entry point and      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 143 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  script the rest; X4 and Star Citizen's traffic control fly authored approach paths, holding point,  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 144 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  approach point, pad, with avoidance relaxed against the station; Elite Dangerous gives a pad and a  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 145 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  permission that lapses, limits speed near a station and flies its docking computer down a fixed     \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 146 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  approach; Space Engineers' general autopilot is known for circling and overshooting its             \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m147\u001b[14G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mwaypoints, the failure here, which players work round with a slow precision mode or scripts. So  \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m148\u001b[14G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mthe solution: an approach corridor flown without stopping, at a speed that falls with the           \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m149\u001b[14G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mdistance left; the station not an obstacle on the corridor's last leg, as it is not on the way      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 150 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  down (`byHull`); Arrive damping the velocity across its line rather than pursuing; and a            \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 151 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  reservation that lapses when a ship stops making progress rather than at a fixed time. Measured by  \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 152 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  ships flown in from every side and speed, one queued behind another on the next pad, and no         \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 153 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  arrival slower than the stopgap's.                                                                  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 154 \u001b[12G\u001b[22m-\u001b[14G**A\u001b[18Gtest\u001b[23Gof\u001b[26Gan\u001b[29Gacquire\u001b[37Gout\u001b[41Gof\u001b[44Gdate\u001b[49Gtwice**\u001b[57G(the\u001b[62Guser's,\u001b[70G2026-11-18).\u001b[83G`drawEveryFrame`'s\u001b[102Grecreate\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m 155 \u001b[12G\u001b[22m  loop and its failure after eigh\u001b[46G are not\u001b[55Gcov\u001b[59Gred: it \u001b[68Geeds fault injection u\u001b[91Gder th\u001b[98G Vulkan\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[2m 156 \u001b[22m   layer,\u001b[21Gwhich\u001b[27Gthe\u001b[31Gengine\u001b[38Gdoes\u001b[43Gnot\u001b[47Ghave.\u001b[53GTaken\u001b[59Gup\u001b[62Gwhen\u001b[67Gthat\u001b[72Gbranch\u001b[79Gis\u001b[82Gneeded,\u001b[90Gif\u001b[93Gever.\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m \u001b[3G\u001b[39mRunn\u001b[11G\u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command…\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m$ sed -n 124,160p '/hom\u001b[30G/ivan/projects/jettison'/docs/roadmap.md\r\u001b[14C\u001b[2B12m 48s · ↓\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m34.9k token\u001b[39G)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[18C\u001b[6B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(shift+tab to cycle) · esc to inte\u001b[54Grupt · ← 1 agent\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
