es: a native Manifest system runs each \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m     -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mship's saved job (choose, travel, buy, travel, sell) through the players' own commands, for a player's\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m     -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m ship and an NPC's alike, no behaviour tree or Wasm policy yet. A lot's cost is what its fills paid, f\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m     -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mees included, shared by its partial sales proportionally, rounded up, the last taking the rest, with o\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m     -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mne loss-allowance counter for the lot, so splitting a sale cannot multiply it. A policy edit applies a\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m     -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mt the job's next decision, held cargo included, allowance spent staying spent. Autopilot is the job's \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m     -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mtravel, NPC trading companies are authored per scenario and run the same executor on their own reports\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m     -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m, and an unknown market is skipped, not scouted. Transport and holding charges are charged from W10 at\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m     -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m nominal values, each venue's own (D-098), by default a 10-credit docking fee paid as a `Travel` start\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m     -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242ms and a 2-credit berth fee each sim\u001b[76Gerth carried as arrears at the venue's\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
