[0.006, "o", "\u001b[H\r\u001b[4B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m←\u001b[4G☒\u001b[6GDocking\u001b[14Gfee\u001b[19G☒\u001b[21GBerth\u001b[27Gfee\u001b[32G☒\u001b[34GArrears\u001b[43G☒\u001b[45GTransit\u001b[53GLS\u001b[56G\u001b[48;2;177;185;249m\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m ✔ Submit \u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m →\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1mReview your answers\r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m│\u001b[4G\u001b[22m●\u001b[6GWhat should a venue's docking fee be based on, and how much? (Today it is a flat 10 credits, paid as a journey\u001b[117Gto\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m│\u001b[6G\u001b[22mthe venue starts. A furs run makes about 4,600.)\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[38;2;78;186;101m→ By pad size (Recommended)\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[2m│\u001b[4G\u001b[22m●\u001b[6GWhat should a docked ship's hourly berth fee be based on? D-047 says it includes connected life support. (Today it\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m  \u001b[6Gis 2 credits a\u001b[21Gsimulation\u001b[32Ghour.)\r\u001b[3C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m→ Pad + occupants (Recommended)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m ● What happens when\u001b[24Ga\u001b[26Gcompany\u001b[34Gcan't\u001b[40Gpay\u001b[44Gits\u001b[48Gberth\u001b[54Garrears?\u001b[63G(Today\u001b[70Gthe\u001b[74Garrears\u001b[82Gare\u001b[86Gtaken\u001b[92Gfirst\u001b[98Geach\u001b[103Ghour\u001b[108Gand\u001b[112Gmust\u001b[117Gbe\r\u001b[1B \u001b[2m│\u001b[22m   fully paid before the ship can leave, so the ship is already held.)\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[38;2;78;186;101m→ Held, then cargo seized (Recommended)\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[2m│\u001b[4G\u001b[22m●\u001b[6GHow\u001b[10Gshould\u001b[17Gthe\u001b[21Glife\u001b[26Gsupport\u001b[34Ga\u001b[