[0.109, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mThe rule is relaxed. Each commit now has to build, pass the\u001b[63Gtests\u001b[69Gof\u001b[72Gthe\u001b[76Gmodules\u001b[84Git\u001b[87Gtouches,\u001b[96Gand\u001b[100Gbe\u001b[103Gclean\u001b[109Gunder\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bclang-tidy\u001b[14Gin\u001b[17Gthe\u001b[21Gfiles\u001b[27Git\u001b[30Gchanged.\u001b[39GThe\u001b[43Gfull\u001b[48Ggate\u001b[53Gruns\u001b[58Gonce\u001b[63Gper\u001b[67Gchunk\u001b[73Gof\u001b[76Gtwo\u001b[80Gor\u001b[83Gthree\u001b[89Gcommits,\u001b[98Gand\u001b[102Gthe\u001b[106Glast\u001b[111Gcommit\u001b[118Gof\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Ga chunk must pass it b\u001b[26Gfore any\u001b[35Ghing\u001b[40Gis\u001b[43Gpushed.\u001b[51GIf\u001b[54Ga\u001b[56Ggate\u001b[61Grun\u001b[65Gfails,\u001b[72GI\u001b[74Gfix\u001b[78Git\u001b[81Gin\u001b[84Ga\u001b[86Gfurther\u001b[94Gcommit\u001b[101Grather\u001b[108Gthan\r\u001b[1B  rewriting history.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mRule text:\u001b[16G\u001b[22mupdated\u001b[24Gin\u001b[27GJettison's\u001b[38G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mdocs/coding-standards.md\u001b[63G\u001b[39m(Commits)\u001b[73Gand\u001b[77Gin\u001b[80G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mAGENTS.md\u001b[39m,\u001b[91Gcommitted\u001b[101Gas\u001b[104GJettison\u001b[113G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m209590e\u001b[39m.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1BThat was a docs-only chang\u001b[32G, so no gate.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mW18 plan:\u001b[22m now says the\u001b[28Ggate runs \u001b[39Gfter sli\u001b[48Ges 3 an\u001b[56G 5. That\u001b[65Gedit goes into slice 3's\u001b[90Gcommit.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mMemory:\u001b[22m saved as \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mgate-per-chunk\u001b[39m, so la\u001b[44Ger se\u001b[50Gsions\u001b[56Gfollow the\u001b[67Gnew rule.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mNot pushed:\u001b[17G\u001b[22mM\u001b[19Gnifest \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mad8f6b3\u001b[39m (slic\u001b[40G 2) and Jettison\u001b[57G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m209590e\u001b[39m.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BNext is\u001b[11Gslice\u001b[17G3,\u001b[20Gthe\u001b[24GAI\u001b[27Goperators'\u001b[38Gdaily\u001b[44Gfee\u001b[48Grule,\u001b[54Gcommitted\u001b[64Gwith\u001b[69Gonly\u001b[74Gits\u001b[78Gown\u001b[82Gtests\u001b[88Gand\u001b[92Gthe\u001b[96Gchanged\u001b[104Gfiles'\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bclang-tidy. The gate then runs once slice 3 is i\u001b[52G. Opus at \u001b[63Gedium\u001b[69Geffort\u001b[76Gis\u001b[79Genough\u001b[86Gfor\u001b[90Git.\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3GThe new\u001b[11Grule now holds in\u001b[29Gboth\u001b[34Grepos,\u001b[41Gand\u001b[45GManifest's\u001b[56Gown\u001b[60Gdocs\u001b[65Gdon't\u001b[71Grestate\u001b[79Git.\u001b[83GThe\u001b[87Grisk:\u001b[93Ga\u001b[95Gcommit\u001b[102Gbetween\u001b[110Ggates\u001b[116Gcould\r\u001b[1B  break something only the address sanitiser or another module's tests would catch. If that happens, the fix arrives as\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Ba\u001b[5Glater commit, so history can briefly hold a commit that fails the gate.\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;44H\u001b[?25h"]
