[0.111, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRecalled \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m memory, wrote \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m memories \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mUnderstood.\u001b[15GI've\u001b[20Gsaved\u001b[26Git\u001b[29Gto\u001b[32Gmemory:\u001b[40Gnothing\u001b[48Gruns\u001b[53Galongside\u001b[63Gclang\u001b[69Gor\u001b[72Gclang-tidy.\u001b[84GI\u001b[86Gread\u001b[91Gthat\u001b[96Gas\u001b[99Gone\u001b[103Gbuild\u001b[109Gor\u001b[112Gtidy\u001b[117Grun\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Go\u001b[5G the machine at \u001b[22G time.\u001b[29GThat run still uses all\u001b[53G24 cores itself. If you meant each run should\u001b[99Gus\u001b[103Gone core\u001b[113Goo,\u001b[117Gtell\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bme.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mChanges to my proposal:\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m- \u001b[1mRunning the\u001b[17Gfour builds at the same time:\u001b[47G\u001b[22mdropped.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mThe second checkout:\u001b[22m kept, but only for writing code\u001b[58Gwhile\u001b[64Gthe\u001b[68Ggate\u001b[73Gruns\u001b[78Gthere.\u001b[85GI\u001b[87Gwouldn't\u001b[96Gbuild\u001b[102Gor\u001b[105Gtest\u001b[110Ganywhere\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Guntil the gate finishes. It s\u001b[35Gill saves\u001b[45Gme idling while the gate runs. Wi\u001b[80Gout it, editing\u001b[96Gthe main\u001b[105Gcheckout du\u001b[117Ging\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Ba gate would change the code being ch\u001b[43Gcked\u001b[48Gha\u001b[51Gfway throug\u001b[63G.\u001b[65G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mThe stage cross-review:\u001b[29G\u001b[22mit only reads \u001b[44Gode\u001b[48Gand runs no compiler,\u001b[70Gso\u001b[73Git\u001b[76Gcan\u001b[80Gstill\u001b[86Grun\u001b[90Gon\u001b[93Gthe\u001b[97Gsecond\u001b[104Gcheckout\u001b[113Gwhile\u001b[119GI\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gwrite code. It doesn't run\u001b[32Gwhile I build.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[