[0.440, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 83 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 84 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m### Gating beside the work                                                                             \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 85 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m                                                                                                       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 86 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mOn Lythir a commit is gated in a second checkout, so the next change is written while the gate         \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 87 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mruns. `build/gate-tree` is a detached worktree with its own presets' build trees, made once with       \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 88 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m`git worktree add --detach build/gate-tree <commit>`; for each commit gated,                           \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 89 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m`git -C build/gate-tree checkout --detach <commit>` and then `build/gate-tree/scripts/ci.sh` with      \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 90 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mthe gate's options. While it runs nothing else builds, runs tests or runs clang-tidy (the user's,      \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 91 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m2026-11-21), so the work beside it is editing alone. A failure is fixed by a later commit, before      \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 92 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mthe push.                                                                                              \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 93 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m                                                                                                       \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m 94 \u001b[22m ## Ma\u001b[17Ghine-specific concurrency\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m 95 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m96 \u001b[22m [\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mD-051\u001b[39m](decision-ledger.md#d-051) distinguish\u001b[57Gs the laptop's resource limit\u001b[87Gfrom\u001b[92Gother\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mThe split\u001b[13Gworks, with the longes\u001b[36G of\u001b[40Gthr\u001b[44Ge test entri\u001b[57Gs\u001b[59Gat\u001b[62G13 s \u001b[68Ggainst 25 s\u001b[80Gfor the whole suite in\u001b[103Gdebug.\u001b[110GI'm\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcommitti\u001b[12Gg,\u001b[15Gthen r\u001b[22Gnning\u001b[30Ge first gate in a second checkou\u001b[63G,\u001b[65Gwhich w\u001b[73Gll be \u001b[80Glow since it\u001b[93Gbu\u001b[96Glds from\u001b[105Gscratch.\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B· summary\u001b[39m  \u001b[15G   \u001b[19G    \u001b[24G  \u001b[27G   \u001b[31G   \u001b[35G    \u001b[40G  \u001b[43G \u001b[45G  \u001b[76G\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
