[0.227, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(~/projects/manifest/docs/build-and-gates.md)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded \u001b[1m13\u001b[22m lines, removed \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m lines\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 77 \u001b[22m Manifest compiles only the engine modules and dependencies it links, plus its packer. Renderer\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 78 \u001b[22m smoke tests remain Jettison's gate. Do not configure Jettison's unsupported install/export path.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 79 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 80 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mClang-tidy is opt-in \u001b[48;2;92;2;0mlocally \u001b[48;2;61;1;0m(`./scripts/ci.sh --tidy`), since it is expensive on the                  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m 81 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mdevelopment laptop. CI enables it.                                                                     \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 80 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mClang-tidy is opt-in (`./scripts/ci.sh --tidy`), since it is expensive on the\u001b[48;2;4;71;0m development laptop.\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 81 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mCI enables it, and so does a gate on Lythir: with its record of clean units, a small change costs      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 82 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mlittle.                                                                                                \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m 83 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 84 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m### Gating beside the work                                                                             \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 85 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m                                                                                                       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 86 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mOn Lythir a commit is gated in a second checkout, so the next change is written while the gate         \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 87 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mruns. `build/gate-tree` is a detached worktree with its own presets' build trees, made once with       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 88 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m`git worktree add --detach build/gate-tree <commit>`; for each commit gated,                           \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 89 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m`git -C build/gate-tree checkout --detach <commit>` and then `build/gate-tree/scripts/ci.sh` with      \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m9\u001b[11G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mthe \u001b[16Ga\u001b[18Ge's\u001b[22Goptions. While it runs not\u001b[49Ging else builds,\u001b[66Gruns t\u001b[73Gsts or runs\u001b[85Gclang-tidy (the user's,\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m9\u001b[11G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m2026-11-21), so the work beside it is editing alone. A failure is fixed by a\u001b[88Glater commit, before\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m9\u001b[11G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mthe push.\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
