[0.131, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mTidy in the gate:\u001b[22m the\u001b[27Ggate now runs with \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m--tidy\u001b[39m, as\u001b[57GCI\u001b[60Gd\u001b[62Ges.\u001b[66GIt skips files that we\u001b[89Ge\u001b[91Gclean and haven't\u001b[109Gchanged\u001b[117G(57\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bof 58 skipped this time). Its first run found one finding left from W10 in \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mPolicy.cpp:673\u001b[39m that CI would have refused\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bon your next push. It's fixed in Manifest \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m1d08379\u001b[39m.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mSecond checkout:\u001b[22m \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mbuild/gate-tree\u001b[38G\u001b[39mi\u001b[40G \u001b[42G separate working\u001b[60Gcopy of Manifest. I poi\u001b[84Gt\u001b[86Git at a commit\u001b[101Gand run the\u001b[113Ggate\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bthere,\u001b[12Gand\u001b[16Gthe\u001b[20Gonly\u001b[25Gwork\u001b[30GI\u001b[32Gdo\u001b[35Gwhile\u001b[41Git\u001b[44Gruns\u001b[49Gis\u001b[52Gediting\u001b[60Gcode.\u001b[66GThe\u001b[70Gfirst\u001b[76Grun\u001b[80Gthere\u001b[86Gtook\u001b[91G15\u001b[94Gminutes\u001b[102Gbecause\u001b[110Git\u001b[113Gbuilt\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Beverything from scratch; it won't need that again. The routine is in \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mdocs/build-and-gates.md\u001b[39m under \"Gating\u001b[112Gbeside\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bthe\u001b[9Gwork\",\u001b[16Gwith\u001b[21Gyour\u001b[26Grule\u001b[31Gthat\u001b[36Gnothing\u001b[44Gbuilds\u001b[51Galongside\u001b[61Git.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  \u001b[1mNot pushed:\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GManifest: \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mad8f6b3\u001b[39m (slice 2),\u001b[34G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mb108190\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m1d08379\u001b[39m.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GJettison:\u001b[15G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m209590e\u001b[39m.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BNext is\u001b[11GW18\u001b[15Gslice\u001b[21G3,\u001b[24Gthe\u001b[28GAI\u001b[31Goperators'\u001b[42Gdaily\u001b[48Gfee\u001b[52Grule,\u001b[58Ggated\u001b[64Gin\u001b[67Gthe\u001b[71Gsecond\u001b[78Gcheckout.\u001b[88GOpus\u001b[93Gat\u001b[96Gmedium\u001b[103Geffort\u001b[110Gis\u001b[113Genough\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bfor it.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3GThe second checkout lives\u001b[29Ginside\u001b[36GManifest's\u001b[47G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mbuild/\u001b[54G\u001b[39mfolder,\u001b[62Gso\u001b[65Gdeleting\u001b[74G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mbuild/\u001b[81G\u001b[39mdeletes\u001b[89Git.\u001b[93GIf\u001b[96Gthat\u001b[101Ghappens,\u001b[110Grun\u001b[114G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mgit \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mworktree prune\u001b[39m and recreate it with the \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mgit worktree add\u001b[39m command in the docs; the next gate there then takes about\u001b[118G15\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bminutes again. It also uses about 14 GB of disk. I didn't run the content suite (60 s under the sanitisers), so I\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bdon't know whether it is now what limits\u001b[44Gthe\u001b[48Gtest\u001b[53Gstage.\r\u001b[26C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m9\u001b[29G3\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
